ich may represent microcalcifications, further support the diagnosis of PTC. Other potential diagnoses, such as follicular carcinoma and medullary carcinoma, are less likely given the specific ultrasound characteristics and the demographic profile of the patient. Overall, the combination of clinical and imaging findings aligns with the typical presentation of papillary thyroid carcinoma, warranting further evaluation through fine needle aspiration biopsy. \n"], "raw_output": "'''Option: D'''"}
