y, surgery, otolaryngology, and neurology. The clinical implications of hoarseness post-surgery are underscored, noting that such symptoms can indicate nerve damage and may lead to serious consequences, including vocal cord paralysis and compromised airway function. The reports collectively stress the importance of careful surgical technique and postoperative monitoring to mitigate these risks and address any complications promptly. \n"], "raw_output": "'''Option: D'''"}
